        "day_number": 131,
        "title": "May 10",
        "content": "<p>Morning</p>\n<p><em>“But now is Christ risen from the dead.”</em></p>\n<p>1 Corinthians 15:20</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial morning reflection:</strong> Christian hope rests in the bodily resurrection of Jesus and God's promise to raise the dead and renew creation. This hope does not silence grief; it gives courage to remain faithful within it.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more before the day gathers pace. Name one concrete way its truth can shape your attention, speech, or action today.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Risen Christ, meet me in grief and hope, and form in me a life that bears witness to your resurrection. Amen.</p>\n<p>Evening</p>\n<p><em>“The only begotten of the Father, full of grace and truth.”</em></p>\n<p>John 1:14</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial evening reflection:</strong> God's mercy is gift, not payment for achievement or respectability. Receive grace without self-contempt, extend it without favoritism, and remember that forgiveness never makes another person's suffering unimportant.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more and review the day without denial or self-contempt. Give thanks, name what needs repair, and entrust tomorrow to God.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Merciful God, let your grace free me from shame and pride, and make me generous in forgiveness, truth, and repair. Amen.</p>",
        "references": [
          "1 Corinthians 15:20",
          "John 1:14"
        ]
      },
