        "day_number": 133,
        "title": "May 12",
        "content": "<p>Morning</p>\n<p><em>“And will manifest myself to him.”</em></p>\n<p>John 14:21</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial morning reflection:</strong> This verse directs our attention to Jesus Christ, the eternal Son who became truly human for our salvation. Receive what it reveals about his character or work, and let trust in him take visible form in love.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more before the day gathers pace. Name one concrete way its truth can shape your attention, speech, or action today.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord Jesus Christ, true God and true human, draw me into your life and teach me to follow you in love. Amen.</p>\n<p>Evening</p>\n<p><em>“Fear not to go down into Egypt; for I will there make of you a great nation: I will go down with you into Egypt; and I will also surely bring you up again.”</em></p>\n<p>Genesis 46:3,4</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial evening reflection:</strong> In Genesis 46:3–4, Jacob is afraid of moving his household to Egypt. God assures him that he will not be abandoned. This is a story of a particular family and its future, not a blanket promise that every journey will be safe or every loss reversed in this lifetime. Pray about a change you face, listen to those who will be affected, and make a practical plan with trusted people. Receive God's presence as a source of courage without treating the people of another land as less worthy of respect.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more and review the day without denial or self-contempt. Give thanks, name what needs repair, and entrust tomorrow to God.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Compassionate God, stay near in suffering, lead me toward wise help, and make me attentive to another person's pain. Amen.</p>",
        "references": [
          "John 14:21",
          "Genesis 46:3,4"
        ]
      },
