        "day_number": 137,
        "title": "May 16",
        "content": "<p>Morning</p>\n<p><em>“Who gives us richly all things to enjoy.”</em></p>\n<p>1 Timothy 6:17</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial morning reflection:</strong> Holiness is life being reshaped by communion with God. It appears in integrity, compassion, self-control, justice, and love rather than contempt for people who struggle or confidence in our own superiority.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more before the day gathers pace. Name one concrete way its truth can shape your attention, speech, or action today.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Holy God, conform me to Christ and make my words, habits, and relationships bear the fruit of your love. Amen.</p>\n<p>Evening</p>\n<p><em>“And he said, Thus says the Lord, Make this valley full of ditches. For thus says the Lord, You shall not see wind, neither shall you see rain; yet that valley shall be filled with water, that you may drink, both you and your cattle, and your beasts.”</em></p>\n<p>2 Kings 3:16,17</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial evening reflection:</strong> Creation is God's good gift, entrusted to human care rather than exploitation. Receive its beauty with gratitude, respect the limits of creatures and ecosystems, and practice stewardship that serves future neighbors too.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more and review the day without denial or self-contempt. Give thanks, name what needs repair, and entrust tomorrow to God.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Creator of heaven and earth, awaken gratitude and teach me to care faithfully for the world and its creatures. Amen.</p>",
