      {
        "day_number": 165,
        "title": "June 13",
        "content": "<p>Morning</p>\n<p><em>“Whoever will, let him take the water of life freely.”</em></p>\n<p>Revelation 22:17</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial morning reflection:</strong> Revelation 22:17 offers the water of life as God's free gift. Spurgeon's original illustration makes the invitation by demeaning sex workers, laborers, and people of different social classes; those comparisons are omitted. No wealth, reputation, education, or respectable appearance purchases grace, and no stigmatized history places a person beyond Christ's welcome. Come honestly, receive mercy as gift, and refuse to build social barriers around the church's invitation.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more before the day gathers pace. Name one concrete way its truth can shape your attention, speech, or action today.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of hope, keep me faithful while I wait and let your promised future strengthen love in the present. Amen.</p>\n<p>Evening</p>\n<p><em>“Remove far from me vanity and lies.”</em></p>\n<p>Proverbs 30:8</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial evening reflection:</strong> Wisdom listens before speaking, tests appearances, welcomes correction, and seeks the good of others. Ask what is true, what love requires, and whose experience needs to be heard before you act.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more and review the day without denial or self-contempt. Give thanks, name what needs repair, and entrust tomorrow to God.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of wisdom, give me a teachable heart, truthful speech, and discernment that produces peace and justice. Amen.</p>",
        "references": [
          "Revelation 22:17",
          "Proverbs 30:8"
        ]
      },
