      {
        "day_number": 268,
        "title": "September 24",
        "content": "<p>Morning</p>\n<p><em>“For I was ashamed to require of the king a band of soldiers and horsemen to help us against the enemy in the way: because we had spoken to the king, saying, The hand of our God is upon all them for good that seek him; but his power and his wrath is against all them that forsake him.”</em></p>\n<p>Ezra 8:22</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial morning reflection:</strong> Ezra 8:21–23 describes a particular decision to fast and pray before a dangerous journey. Spurgeon's application warns against depending on human help, but should not be read as advice to refuse security, medical care, or other practical assistance. The Bible also commends wise counsel and planning (Proverbs 15:22). Trust in God and appropriate human help can work together. Pray about a need today and take one responsible step, including asking others for assistance when necessary.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more before the day gathers pace. Name one concrete way its truth can shape your attention, speech, or action today.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Righteous and merciful Christ, keep me watchful, humble, and active in love as I await your kingdom. Amen.</p>\n<p>Evening</p>\n<p><em>“I sleep, but my heart wakes.”</em></p>\n<p>Song of Solomon 5:2</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial evening reflection:</strong> Love of God takes shape in patient, truthful care for neighbors, family, strangers, and the church. Healthy love respects conscience and boundaries; it does not excuse harm or demand silence from those who suffer.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more and review the day without denial or self-contempt. Give thanks, name what needs repair, and entrust tomorrow to God.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of communion, teach me to love with truth, patience, courage, and respect for every person's dignity. Amen.</p>",
        "references": [
          "Ezra 8:22",
          "Song of Solomon 5:2"
        ]
      },
