        "day_number": 279,
        "title": "October 5",
        "content": "<p>Morning</p>\n<p><em>“He arose, and did eat and drink, and went in the strength of that food forty days and forty nights.”</em></p>\n<p>1 Kings 19:8</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial morning reflection:</strong> Faith is not denial of evidence, pain, or honest questions. It is a growing reliance on God's character that can seek wisdom, receive help, and take the next faithful step without pretending certainty we do not have.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more before the day gathers pace. Name one concrete way its truth can shape your attention, speech, or action today.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Trustworthy God, hold me amid uncertainty and guide my next step in wisdom, courage, and love. Amen.</p>\n<p>Evening</p>\n<p><em>“He that believes and is baptized shall be saved.”</em></p>\n<p>Mark 16:16</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial evening reflection:</strong> This verse directs our attention to Jesus Christ, the eternal Son who became truly human for our salvation. Receive what it reveals about his character or work, and let trust in him take visible form in love.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more and review the day without denial or self-contempt. Give thanks, name what needs repair, and entrust tomorrow to God.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord Jesus Christ, true God and true human, draw me into your life and teach me to follow you in love. Amen.</p>",
