      {
        "day_number": 354,
        "title": "December 19",
        "content": "<p>Morning</p>\n<p><em>“The lot is cast into the lap, but the whole disposing of it is of the Lord.”</em></p>\n<p>Proverbs 16:33</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial morning reflection:</strong> Wisdom listens before speaking, tests appearances, welcomes correction, and seeks the good of others. Ask what is true, what love requires, and whose experience needs to be heard before you act.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more before the day gathers pace. Name one concrete way its truth can shape your attention, speech, or action today.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of wisdom, give me a teachable heart, truthful speech, and discernment that produces peace and justice. Amen.</p>\n<p>Evening</p>\n<p><em>“And there was no more sea.”</em></p>\n<p>Revelation 21:1</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial evening reflection:</strong> Creation is God's good gift, entrusted to human care rather than exploitation. Receive its beauty with gratitude, respect the limits of creatures and ecosystems, and practice stewardship that serves future neighbors too.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more and review the day without denial or self-contempt. Give thanks, name what needs repair, and entrust tomorrow to God.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Creator of heaven and earth, awaken gratitude and teach me to care faithfully for the world and its creatures. Amen.</p>",
        "references": [
          "Proverbs 16:33",
          "Revelation 21:1"
        ]
      },
